# The fixes to step 28 from its full review, the approvals part, after
# the pre-push review of its pull request: a command's front matter refuses
# a key after a quoted value, in a quote or a flow collection never closed,
# and less indented than a block, and takes no `: ` inside quotes or a flow
# collection for a key. (The part's first breaks are in
# `step-28-fixes.breaks`; these take the place of its
# `front-matter-folds-a-key-into-a-value` and
# `front-matter-refuses-a-quoted-value`, whose code is gone.)

[break] front-matter-folds-a-key-into-a-plain-value
rule: A command's front matter refuses a plain value that goes on onto a line holding a `key: ` of its own, which YAML refuses: a `profile` indented after a field is not folded into that field.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: not_the_values
find: .filter(|text| said(text) && holds_a_key(text.trim_start()))
replace: .filter(|text| said(text) && holds_a_key(text.trim_start()) && false)
caught-by:
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_written_indented_is_not_passed_over
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_not_passed_over
    cineris-ext skills::tests::what_a_strict_reader_refuses_is_told_and_a_skill_reads_as_before

[break] front-matter-passes-a-key-after-a-quote
rule: A line after the one where a quoted value closes is refused: `description: "Ship it"` then `  profile: careful` does not read as "Ship it" with no profile.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: not_the_values
find: Some(closed) => more[closed..]
replace: Some(closed) => more[closed.max(more.len())..]
caught-by:
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_not_passed_over
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_told_and_a_skill_reads_as_before

[break] front-matter-takes-an-unclosed-quote
rule: A quoted value never closed is refused, not read as far as it goes with the keys after it inside.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: not_the_values
find: None => vec![line.to_owned()]
replace: None => Vec::new()
occurrence: 1
caught-by:
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_not_passed_over
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_told_and_a_skill_reads_as_before

[break] front-matter-folds-a-less-indented-line-into-a-block
rule: A line of a `|` or `>` block indented less than the block is refused, not folded into it.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: not_the_values
find: .filter(|text| said(text) && leading(text) < indent)
replace: .filter(|text| said(text) && leading(text) < indent && false)
caught-by:
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_not_passed_over
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_told_and_a_skill_reads_as_before

[break] front-matter-takes-an-unclosed-flow
rule: A flow collection never closed is refused, not read with the keys after it inside.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: not_the_values
find: None => return vec![line.to_owned()]
replace: None => return Vec::new()
caught-by:
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_not_passed_over

[break] front-matter-takes-a-flows-item-for-a-key
rule: Nothing inside a flow collection over several lines is taken for a key.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: not_the_values
find: Some(closed) => after = closed
replace: Some(_) => after = 0
caught-by:
    cineris-ext skills::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_told_and_a_skill_reads_as_before

[break] front-matter-takes-a-colon-in-quotes-for-a-key
rule: A `: ` inside a quoted text that closes on its line is no key: a default `"a: b"` on a flow list's second line is not refused.
file: crates/cineris-ext/src/skills.rs
in: holds_a_key
find: if let Some(length) = closed_on_the_line(&rest, character) {
replace: if let Some(length) = closed_on_the_line(&rest, character).filter(|_| false) {
caught-by:
    cineris-ext commands::tests::a_key_after_a_quote_or_a_block_is_not_passed_over

[break] front-matter-closes-a-quote-at-its-escape
